BIB                 18         75
TITLE       Neutron activation cross-sections at (14.6+-0.3) MeV
AUTHOR     (H.M.Agrawal, Kailash Pandey, K.Surendra Babu,
           Ashok Kumar, R.Pepelnik)
INSTITUTE  (2GERKIG)  Institute of Physics, GKSS Research Centre,
             Geesthacht, Germany. R.Pepelnik, experimental site
           (3INDIND)  Physics Department, G.B. Pant University,
             Pantnagar 263 145, India. H.M.Agrawal, Corresponding
             author. E-mail address: hma001@rediffmail.com;
             K.Pandey
           (3KORKAE)  Nuclear Data Evaluation Lab KAERI,
             South Korea.  K.Surendra Babu
           (3INDTRM)   Reactor Physics Design Division, BARC,
             Trombay, Mumbai, India. A.Kumar
REFERENCE  (J,ANE,35,1713,2008)
           #doi:10.1016/j.anucene.2008.02.004
                                Main reference, data are given
REL-REF    (M,,H.M.Agrawal+,J,NIM/A,366,349,1995) H.M.Agrawal,
              R.Pepelnik, method of neutron energy determination
           (I,,R.Pepelnik+,J,JRC,72,393,1982) J. of Radioanal.
             Chem., v.72,p.393-403. R.Pepelnik et al.,
              experimental details
           (I,,R.Pepelnik+,J,NIM/A,226,411,1984)  Nucl. Instrum.
             Methods, v. 226,p.411. R.Pepelnik et al.,
             Experimental details
           (I,,H.-U.Fanger+,J,JRC,61,147,1981) J. of Radioanal.
            Chemistry, v. 61, p. 147, 1981. Experimental details
FACILITY   (ACCEL,2GERKIG)  High-intensity neutron generator
            KORONA with a usable fast neutron flux of 3.x 10**12
            n/cm2/s, a fast rabbit system suitable for cyclic
            irradiations and measurements for short-lived
            activities.
INC-SOURCE (D-T)  A mixed D-T gas are accelerated towards an inner
             target cylinder (80 * 42 mm) and react with hydrogen
             isotopes of the self-regenerating Sc-TD gas. Beam
             current is 340 milli-A, accelerating voltage 180 MV
INC-SPECT  .Narrow 14 MeV neutron beam, neutron flux
            3.E+10 n/cm2/sec +- 5%. (Zr/Nb) and Ni-foil activation
            methods used for neutron energy determination which
            is 14.6 +- 0.3 MeV
METHOD     (ACTIV,COINC) Activation, coincidence
           (SITA)  The standard solution of known mass is filled
             into the capsules of the same type are used in
             actual irradiation.
PART-DET   (G,N)
DETECTOR   (GELI)  Ge(Li) detector with a relative efficiency of
             17% is used for gamma detection at a distance of
             56.5 mm from the sample
           (LONGC) For neutron flux determination
MONITOR    (13-AL-27(N,A)11-NA-24,,SIG)
           .A homogeneously mixed STANDARD solution of radioactive
            sources containing 54Mn, 57Co, 88Y, 133Ba, 137Cs
            isotopes,  emitting c-rays of 80.9, 122.1, 136.5,
            276.4, 302.9, 356.0, 383.8, 661.6, 634.8, 898.0,
            1836.0 keV, respectively.
MONIT-REF  (,G.Winkler+,J,ANE,10,601,1983)  G.Winkler,T.B.Ryves,
               Annals Nucl.Energy, 10 (11), 601, 1983.
SAMPLE     .Powdered as well as liquid samples are irradiated on
            the axis of thin cylindrical target in polyethylene
            containers (7 * 10 mm)
CORRECTION .For coincidence summing
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T)  Total error
           (ERR-1,0.1,3.)  error of the peak area estimation.
           (ERR-2)  Error in flux and gamma-ray efficiency
                    calibration
           (ERR-3,1.,2.)  summing correction error.
           .Gamma ray intensity errors are taken into account
            individually
STATUS     (TABLE)  From Table 2 of ANE,35,1713
HISTORY    (20081017C)   SM
           (20110206A) SD: DOI identifier was corrected. Refs.
           moved to REF-REF:  Nucl.Instr.& Methods A366,349,1995;
            J. of Radioanal.Chem., 72, 393,1982;
            Nucl.Instr.& Methods 226,411, 1984
           (20131215U) SD: INSTITUTE=3KORPUE -> 3KORKAE ("Pohang"
           in the article is incorrect, Y.O.Lee, 2013-11-07).
ENDBIB              75
COMMON               3          3
EN         EN-ERR     ERR-2
MEV        MEV        PER-CENT
   14.6       0.3          3.
